From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:31:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Remove tool: paint over an object to remove it (AI)

Photoshop's Remove tool (GimpRemoveTool, a GimpDrawTool), in the J group:
paint over an object, the strokes shown in Photoshop's see-through pink
with the brush outline under the pointer; on release (or Enter, without
Tool Options' Remove after each stroke; Escape clears) it runs GIMPhoto's
plug-in procedure gimphoto-remove with the strokes as JSON and the model
(LaMa, or FLUX.2 klein with Generative fill), from an idle callback once
the event is done, one removal at a time, the image, display and drawable
kept alive until it returns. [ and ] change the brush size
(tools-remove-size-set).

